    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0325" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg251"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 30, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your despatch of the 28th
                    ultimo, No. 40, and to my reply of the 23d instant, No. 79, in regard to
                    insurgent piratical movements and schemes in Europe, I have now to inform you
                    that, by a letter of yesterday, the Secretary of the Navy informs me that the
                    Kearsarge, now at Boston, has been ordered to proceed to the coast of Europe for
                    the purpose of co-operating with the vessels now engaged in watching the
                    movements of the Stonewall, and will use all possible despatch in reaching her
                    destination.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWED.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c. Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
